 "keyingConvention": "'keyed' is relative to the ZEHN scale code. IPIP scores Factor IV as Emotional Stability; ZEHN codes it as N (Neuroticism), so every Factor IV item's key is flipped: an item IPIP keys '-' for Emotional Stability (e.g., 'Get stressed out easily.') is '+' for N. The original IPIP key is kept in 'ipipKeyed' and the IPIP factor number in 'ipipFactor'. To report Emotional Stability instead, score ES = 6*10 - N_sum on a 1-5 response scale (i.e., reverse N). Factor V is labelled 'O' but the UI must show 'Openness/Intellect' because the IPIP marker emphasises intellect.",
